# MiniMax-M3.1-Flash on two NVIDIA DGX Sparks (TP=2 over the CX7 link) with TensorFold v1.1.2's native engine and the
# minimax_m3_vl family: the production profile. scripts/config.sh reads it for every script (start.sh, stop.sh,
# scripts/serve.sh, scripts/prepare.sh, scripts/watch.sh); KEY=value lines, read, never run.
#
#   cp config/prod.env.example config/prod.env      on the head only (the worker needs no copy of this repository)
#
# Fill in the <placeholders> (scripts refuse to run while one is left; AGENTS.md section 3 says how to find each value) and
# leave the rest. Where a value comes from: (calc) scripts/quant_budget.py --serve for this pack and profile, not a
# measurement; (DS) / (GLM) the DeepSeek-V4.1 / GLM-5.3 recipes' measured setting; (Mia) MiaAI-Lab's base recipe; (pin) a
# verified revision. NOTHING in this profile has served the model on two Sparks yet: docs/KNOWN-ISSUES.md.
# A caller export wins over this file: CONTEXT=65536 scripts/serve.sh restart. The full list with defaults is
# scripts/config.sh; this file names every setting an operator may need.

# -- nodes -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This Spark (the head) serves rank 0 and the API; WORKER is the other Spark (rank 1), key-based ssh, no password.
# The worker's address on the CX7 link is best: the checkpoint copy (WEIGHTS=local) goes over the route to it.
WORKER="<user@worker-link-address>"
# FABRIC_PEER=                   # the worker's CX7 address, when WORKER is a LAN address (the ranks then still use the link)
# Pin the link (GLM's check; empty: whatever the route to the worker uses). The names come from `ibdev2netdev` (RDMA device
# ==> netdev, for the cabled port) on this Spark; start and preflight refuse when the detected link differs.
LINK_NETDEV=
LINK_HCAS=
MASTER_PORT=29620                # NCCL_COMM_ID's port on the head's link address; MASTER_PORT + 1 must be free too (Mia)
NCCL_RAILS=2                     # both PCIe twins of the cabled CX7 port, each probed before use; 1: one rail (Mia)

# -- checkpoint (pin) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# jayleaton's EXL3 pack, 199.9 GB (26 shards + dspark/), private (hf auth login on the head). Its LICENSE is the MiniMax
# Community License: read it before serving or sharing anything.
MODEL_ID=jayleaton/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-EXL3-3.55bpw-mm31
MODEL_REVISION=5bff3d732e9dfa236a41b6f3054dd8550bef595f
# HF_CACHE=                      # this Spark's Hugging Face cache (default ~/.cache/huggingface; needs ~220 GB free)
# WEIGHTS=local: a byte-identical copy in the worker's own HF cache, copied over ssh by scripts/serve.sh prepare (GLM, DS).
# WEIGHTS=nfs: the worker reads this Spark's cache over NFS (Mia; NFS_PATH, NFS_SERVER, NFS_VOLUME in scripts/config.sh).
# WEIGHTS=dir: each Spark already holds the pack as a plain folder (hf download --local-dir, or a copy): MODEL_DIR here,
# WORKER_MODEL_DIR there; mounted read-only at /model, checked (shards, size, SHA256SUMS here, the worker's by size), never copied.
WEIGHTS=local
# WORKER_HF_CACHE=               # the worker's cache, when it is not its ~/.cache/huggingface ($HF_HOME)
# MODEL_DIR=                     # WEIGHTS=dir: this Spark's folder of the pack (absolute, or ~/... in each node's own home)
# WORKER_MODEL_DIR=              # WEIGHTS=dir: the worker's folder (default: MODEL_DIR)

# -- engine ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TensorFold v1.1.2 (TF_REF in scripts/config.sh) plus engine/patches: MiaAI-Lab's minimax_m3_vl family (patches/0001,
# unchanged) and the engine this profile was measured with on top of it (engine/SOURCE-EXPORT.md). ENGINE_COMMIT is the
# engine commit that series was exported from (scripts/export-engine.sh). scripts/serve.sh build rebuilds the image when
# either changes. ENGINE_PATCHES=patches builds MiaAI-Lab's family alone.
ENGINE_PATCHES=engine/patches
ENGINE_COMMIT=0547afe802fa402edc87f0d399b72ff8edb49c38
# 1: the engine has mm3/api-tools (tool_choice "required" / named, response_format, thinking off, thinking_budget, the five
# effort levels): the canary and the bench harnesses fail on a refusal instead of skipping it. The engine above has it.
ENGINE_API_TOOLS=1
# TF_MM3_GRAPHS_TP=1 also captures the two ranks' exchanges in CUDA graphs (measured on in window-all-3); 0: graphs stay
# off at TP2. It is in the ranks' fingerprint: both ranks get the same value.
TF_MM3_GRAPHS_TP=1
IMAGE=tensorfold-minimax-m3:v1.1.2
CONTAINER_NAME=minimax-m3-flash-tf   # the same name on both Sparks

# -- API ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERVED_NAME=MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-EXL3
HOST=127.0.0.1                   # loopback only: no auth (GLM, DS). HOST=0.0.0.0 only with API_KEY=1 or a proxy with auth
PORT=8000                        # 8001 when the guard front serves 8000 (docs/OPERATIONS.md, Guard)
API_KEY=0                        # 1: rank 0 requires a key from API_KEY_FILE (mode 600, generated when missing; never argv)
# API_KEY_FILE=                  # default ~/.local/state/tensorfold-minimax-m3/api-key

# -- serving profile ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The profile measured in window-all-3 (results/window-all-3): 131,072 x 1, FP8 KV, the dspark draft, from the calculator
#   python3 scripts/quant_budget.py --serve --context 131072 --parallel 1 --kv fp8 --reserve-gib 8 --drafter dspark
# 92.66 GiB of weights a rank plus the draft, MEM_GATE_GIB 115. PARALLEL=4 is measured too (config/slots4.env.example):
# 52.0 tok/s aggregate on code with drafts at depth 3 (window-all-3), 65.5 with drafts off (window-all-2), every concurrent
# reply equal to its alone reply (MEM_GATE_GIB 117). 4 x 1M needs the engine's KV tier (below), which starts but panics at
# the first prompt: opt-in, off.
CONTEXT=131072                   # tokens a request holds (prompt + reply); the base model declares 1,048,576 (calc)
PARALLEL=1                       # requests at once; raise only after the concurrent == solo check (docs/OPERATIONS.md)
MAX_TOKENS=32768                 # a reply's budget when a request sets none (GLM, DS)
# fp8: K and V as e4m3 rows with an fp32 scale per token and kv head, index keys bf16: 47,040 B a token a rank instead of
# 76,800 (Mia's patches/tasks/0016; the calculator's KV_RANK_FP8). Its effect on answers is NOT MEASURED; bf16 is the fallback.
KV=fp8
# The KV tier (engine mm3/kv-tier, docs/receipts/mm3-kv-tier): every page on this NVMe folder, one O_DIRECT file a rank,
# mounted at /kvtier in both ranks (WORKER_KV_TIER_DIR on the worker, default the same path). start.sh refuses to start
# unless both disks have TF_MM3_KV_TIER_GIB free plus KV_TIER_KEEP_GIB. Empty KV_TIER_DIR (the default): no tier.
# Exact (TF_MM3_KV_HORIZON empty: the whole context scored exactly, only K/V on NVMe), e.g. CONTEXT=262144 PARALLEL=1:
#   KV_TIER_DIR=~/.local/state/tensorfold-minimax-m3/kvtier TF_MM3_KV_TIER=/kvtier TF_MM3_KV_TIER_GIB=64
# Approximate 4 x 1M (opt-in; answer quality NOT MEASURED), CONTEXT=1048576 PARALLEL=4 MEM_GATE_GIB=112:
#   ... TF_MM3_KV_TIER_GIB=252 TF_MM3_KV_HORIZON=32768 TF_MM3_KV_CANDIDATES=16 (scripts/quant_budget.py --serve --kv-tier)
KV_TIER_DIR=
WORKER_KV_TIER_DIR=
KV_TIER_KEEP_GIB=300             # disk each Spark keeps free beyond the tier's file
# TF_MM3_KV_TIER: /kvtier with KV_TIER_DIR (the folder inside the containers); TF_MM3_KV_TIER_GIB: NVMe a rank (calc);
# TF_MM3_KV_HORIZON: tokens scored exactly, empty for the whole context; TF_MM3_KV_CANDIDATES: cold pages a kv head
# reranks past the horizon (empty: 16)
TF_MM3_KV_TIER=
TF_MM3_KV_TIER_GIB=
TF_MM3_KV_HORIZON=
TF_MM3_KV_CANDIDATES=
# Prepared per-rank weights (an engine that reads TF_MM3_PREPARED; one without it ignores both variables). PREPARED=1 mounts
# each node's folder at /prepared and gives both ranks TF_MM3_PREPARED=/prepared and TF_MM3_PREPARED_WRITE=1: a boot that
# finds no file for its key writes mm3-r<rank>of<world>-<key16>.tfprep (~94 GiB a rank), later boots read it. A new pack
# revision, engine build or layout setting is a new key (the old file is stale: scripts/serve.sh prepared clean). The
# switch is on for both ranks or neither (both get the same variables); each folder holds its own rank's file only.
# PREPARED=0                     # 1: per-rank prepared files (docs/OPERATIONS.md, Prepared weights)
# HEAD_PREPARED=                 # this Spark's folder (default $CACHE_DIR/prepared, ~/.cache/tensorfold-minimax-m3/prepared)
# WORKER_PREPARED=               # the worker's (default ~/.cache/tensorfold-minimax-m3/prepared in its home; absolute or ~/)
# PREPARED_FREE_GIB=100          # preflight and start want this free on a node whose folder has no file yet
# TF_MM3_PREPARED_WRITE=1        # 0: read a file that is there, never write one (TF_MM3_PREPARED is set by PREPARED=1)
# PROMPT_CACHE_GIB=              # --prompt-cache-gib; empty: the engine's default (Mia)
# THINKING=                      # 1 --thinking, 0 --no-thinking, empty: the template's adaptive mode
# Drafts (measured, results/window-all-3): the pack's own dspark draft, each round's depth sized by its own confidences.
# Replies equal plain decode's (every hash); code, tool calls and math decode +56-74 % over all switches off, prose about
# the same. DRAFTS=0 DRAFTER= turns it off.
DRAFTS=1                         # 1: copy drafts plus DRAFTER; verified, so replies equal plain decode
DRAFTER=dspark                   # dspark: the pack's own draft on both ranks (2.19 GiB a rank: --serve --drafter prices it)
TF_MM3_DSPARK_STATS=1            # rank 0 logs the draft's acceptance per request (docs/DRAFTS.md); as measured
TF_MM3_DSPARK_CHANCES=1          # each round's depth by the draft's confidences against the verify costs (as measured)
TF_MM3_CALIB=auto                # the verify costs: a matching cached table, else timed at boot (+~28 s to the load)
# TF_MM3_DRAFT_DEPTH=            # unset (as measured): the draft's own block caps a round; 1..7 caps it lower (docs/DRAFTS.md)
# DRAFTS=dflash2: copies + the DFlash2 draft (DRAFTER then defaults to dflash2), for the measurement window (docs/DFLASH2.md).
# Its folder: incoai/MiniMax-M3.1-Flash-DFlash2 @ ac07a7c1, 4.2 GB, fetched and checked against
# its sha256 pins by scripts/prepare.sh (--dflash2: only that), mounted read-only at /dflash2 in both ranks. Default: beside the
# pack (WEIGHTS=dir: MODEL_DIR's parent folder; else each node's HF cache under dflash2/). 3.11-3.17 GiB a rank before KV:
# scripts/quant_budget.py --serve --drafter dflash2 gives MEM_GATE_GIB with it (115 for this profile).
# DFLASH2_DIR=                   # this Spark's folder (absolute or ~/)
# WORKER_DFLASH2_DIR=            # the worker's (default: DFLASH2_DIR when set, else beside the worker's pack)
# The RoCE failure marker (mm3/robust): a failed RoCE gather writes it in the node's cache volume (CACHE_VOL, at /cache)
# and the next start of both ranks uses NCCL. scripts/serve.sh roce-reset deletes it once the link is fixed.
TF_ROCE_MARK=/cache/roce-failed
ROCE=1                           # RoCE small gathers when their setup succeeds (else NCCL); 0: NCCL only. Both ranks alike
# ROCE_MAX_KB=                   # TF_ROCE_MAX_KB; empty: the engine's 4096
# The RoCE transport switches (measured on: every reply bit-identical; +4 % plain decode in window-all-2, within noise with
# drafts on in window-all-3). Like every TF_MM3_* and TF_ROCE_* they reach both ranks; 0 or empty turns each off.
TF_MM3_ROCE_SUM=1                # the rank-order fp32 sum fused into the RoCE gather
TF_MM3_SHARE_INPLACE=1           # prompt shares gathered in place
TF_ROCE_FAST=1                   # the lean doorbell
# Image input: OFF. VISION=1 needs ENGINE_COMMIT including the engine branch mm3/vision (an engine without it refuses
# --vision at start). The vision tower loads and runs on rank 0 only: ~2.27 GiB with its scratch and its first call's
# plans on the head, plus every rank's image rows (PARALLEL x VISION_IMAGE_TOKENS x 12 KiB); the engine takes both out of
# the KV room, which both ranks size to rank 0's, so MEM_GATE_GIB does not move. With the KV tier that room is the slice
# cache: `--kv-tier --vision-image-tokens 2304` leaves 5.26 GiB of it at 117.1 GiB available (1.82 needed) but 0.16 at
# MEM_GATE_GIB 112, short (not checked with an engine carrying both mm3/vision and mm3/kv-tier). All-resident, the pool no
# longer holds CONTEXT at 110-113 GiB: docs/OPERATIONS.md section 3a (23680 at 110). An image is at most 576 tokens
# (672 x 672 pixels, 28 x 28 pixels a token); JPEG, PNG and WebP; video parts and other formats are refused with HTTP
# 400. Check it with bench/vision.py smoke (docs/OPERATIONS.md, Images).
VISION=0                         # 1: --vision on both ranks; 0: text only (no tower loaded, an image part gets HTTP 400)
VISION_MAX_IMAGES=4              # --vision-max-images: images a request at most (the engine's default)
VISION_IMAGE_TOKENS=2304         # --vision-image-tokens: a request's images together; 4 x 576 keeps every image at full size
VISION_URLS=0                    # 1: --vision-urls on rank 0 (the head downloads public https images); 0: data: URLs only

# -- memory (docs/OPERATIONS.md, Memory). One value for both ranks: both Sparks have the same MemTotal (DS PR #79) ---------
# What the engine leaves free when it sizes the KV pool, on both ranks. Unset, the engine takes a tenth of MemTotal
# (12.2 GiB), which leaves this pack ~6 GiB of KV a rank; 8 sits above the guard's 4 GiB STOP plus the ~3 GiB serving dip
# the DeepSeek recipe measured (calc, DS).
TENSORFOLD_MEMORY_RESERVE_GIB=8
# The engine's memory floor (needs ENGINE_COMMIT including mm3/robust; an older engine ignores these). Both ranks get the
# same values (they are in the ranks' fingerprint: a mismatch refuses the start). Every chunk gathers both ranks'
# MemAvailable: none starts under the hard floor; a new prompt waits under the target while other streams run; a chunk may
# take the transient beyond its preallocated scratch. The engine's own defaults; the hard floor equals the guard's STOP.
TF_MM3_FLOOR_HARD_GIB=4
TF_MM3_FLOOR_GIB=5
TF_MM3_FLOOR_TRANSIENT_GIB=0.5
MEM_GATE_GIB=115                 # MemAvailable after a drop, both Sparks, before a load (calc for the profile with the dspark draft)
MEM_GATE_TIMEOUT=600             # s the gate waits (dropping the page cache) before the start stops (GLM, DS)
# MEM_GATE_SLACK_GIB=4           # ... and MemFree at least MEM_GATE_GIB - this (the page cache is GPU memory on GB10)
MEM_GATE_DROP_CACHES=1           # drop the page cache while the gate waits; needs the scoped sudo line (AGENTS.md)
DROP_CACHES=1                    # drop it before the load, after the server answers and after the canary (DS)
MEMGUARD_GIB=3                   # memguard kills a rank held under this MemAvailable for MEMGUARD_HOLD_S s (Mia, raised)
MEMGUARD_HOLD_S=4
MEMGUARD_HARD_GIB=2.75           # ... or at once under this: above earlyoom's 2.43 GiB SIGTERM (-m 2 on 124.6 GiB)

# -- temperature: NOT set here. The heat and GPU limits belong to each machine (/etc/spark/thermal.env, installed with
# scripts/install-device-limits.sh); every script reads them from there, start.sh refuses without them, and this file
# may not define GUARD_* (docs/OPERATIONS.md section 4).

# -- the pair and the start --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAIR_WATCH=1                     # stop the surviving rank within PAIR_WATCH_S s when the other exits (DS fail-fast, outside)
PAIR_WATCH_S=5
CANARY=strict                    # scripts/canary.py after the load; strict stops both ranks on a failure (DS)
WAIT_TIMEOUT=2400                # s for /v1/models after the launch; Mia's first TP2 load took 1874 s before her loader fix
PREFLIGHT=strict                 # scripts/serve.sh start runs preflight first; warn: start anyway; off
# GUARD_CONFIG=                  # the guard's JSON (docs/OPERATIONS.md, Guard): start and the watchdog obey it

# -- watchdog (scripts/watch.sh, run by scripts/systemd/tf-watchdog.timer as scripts/serve.sh watch --once) --------------------
WATCH_HEAL=0                     # 1: restart both ranks (scripts/serve.sh restart) after WATCH_FAILS bad ticks
WATCH_FAILS=3
WATCH_MIN_HEAL=1800              # s between heals; a fail-fast record heals on the first tick, every WATCH_FF_MIN_HEAL s
WATCH_FF_MIN_HEAL=120
WATCH_GRACE=2400                 # a rank 0 younger than this that does not answer yet is loading, not bad
# WATCH_LEASE=                   # a file you touch while you benchmark or maintain the pair: the watchdog stands down
# WATCH_ALERT=                   # a command called with a message on every alert

# -- the rest: every other setting the scripts read, at its default (scripts/config.sh says more on each) ------------------
# files and logs
# CONFIG=config/prod.env         # this file (set it in the environment to read another)
# CACHE_VOL=minimax-m3-flash-cache   # each node's docker volume at /cache in its rank (the RoCE marker)
# SPARK_THERMAL_ENV=/etc/spark/thermal.env   # where the device keeps its limits (read, never defined here)
# SPARK_THERMAL_RUN=/run/spark-thermal       # where spark-thermal-guard.service publishes the node's state
# STATE_DIR=                     # ~/.local/state/tensorfold-minimax-m3: locks, prepared marker, stop / fail-fast records
# CACHE_DIR=                     # ~/.cache/tensorfold-minimax-m3 (here and on the worker): saved logs, memguard copy
# LOG_DIR=                       # $CACHE_DIR/logs: each rank's log is saved (gzipped) before its container is removed
# LOG_KEEP=10                     # saved rank logs kept a rank (stop.sh), and gzipped generations a rotated log (logrotate.sh)
# HF_TOKEN_FILE=                 # where `hf auth login` saved the token: only tested for existence, never read or sent
# HF_TOKEN=                      # an alternative to the file, for prepare.sh's `hf download` on this Spark only
# HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1               # the ranks never reach the Hub
# NFS_PATH= NFS_SERVER= NFS_VOLUME=minimax-m3-flash-hf   # WEIGHTS=nfs only
# checkpoint checks (the pins above select these; 0 skips a check for another MODEL_ID)
# MODEL_SHARDS=26
# MODEL_TOTAL_BYTES=197542720916 # the index's total_size
# MODEL_GIB=186.2                # messages only
# MODEL_LICENSE_FILE=LICENSE
# SHA=0                          # 1: prepare.sh checks SHA256SUMS again (it does once per revision)
# engine build (zig/Dockerfile)
# TF_REPO=https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold.git
# TF_TAG=v1.1.2
# TF_REF=4ff784410f70b95767684d337e59dfd6d94fec8b
# ZIG_VERSION=0.17.0
# ZIG_SHA256=9e8d11661d4ae3bd57702a3832781e23ad151dde5798e16a5ccd503f65234ff8
# BASE_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:26.07-py3
# SM=121
# REQUIRED_FAMILY=minimax_m3_vl
# ALLOW_UNSUPPORTED=0            # 1: go on without the family (engine development only; the load fails)
# GHCR_IMAGE= IMAGE_TAG= IMAGE_DIGEST= TAG_BASE=v1.1.2 PULL=1   # a published image (none is published)
# ranks and link
# MASTER_ADDR=                   # the rendezvous address; default the head's address on the link
# SOCKET_IFNAME=                 # NCCL's bootstrap netdev; default the link's
# EXTRA_ENV=                     # NAME=value words for both ranks (a family patch's switches)
# NCCL_DEBUG=                    # passed to both ranks when set (every other exported NCCL_* is too, except the link's own)
# start and stop
# PREPARE=auto                   # 1 forces scripts/prepare.sh before a start, 0 skips it
# FOREGROUND=0                   # 1: stay on rank 0's log and exit with its code (for a supervisor)
# DRY_RUN=0                      # 1: print both ranks' docker commands (scripts/serve.sh args); start nothing
# STOP_TIMEOUT=30                # s a rank gets to stop
# LOG_MAX_SIZE=200m LOG_MAX_FILE=3   # docker's json log of each rank, capped (DS)
# TAIL=80                        # lines scripts/serve.sh logs prints
# boot start (scripts/boot-start.sh, scripts/systemd/mm31-boot-start.service) and log rotation (scripts/logrotate.sh)
# BOOT_WAIT=300                  # s it waits for docker, the worker and the link before it leaves the start to the watchdog
# BOOT_LEASE= BOOT_LEASE_MIN=20  # a file you touch while working on the pair: no start at boot while it is fresh
# BOOT_UNIT=mm31-serve.service   # started when installed (its ExecStop stops the pair at shutdown); empty: serve.sh restart
# BOOT_DRY_RUN=0 BOOT_STDOUT=0   # 1: decide and wait, start nothing / log to the terminal, not STATE_DIR/boot-start.log
# LOG_ROTATE_MIB=16              # a log over this many MiB is rotated (LOG_KEEP gzipped generations, copytruncate)
# watchdog details
# WATCH_STATE_DIR=               # $STATE_DIR/watch
# WATCH_INTERVAL=60              # s between ticks in the foreground loop (the timer runs one tick a minute)
# WATCH_LEASE_MIN=20
# WATCH_RESTART_CMD=             # default scripts/serve.sh restart
# WATCH_BASE= WATCH_PORT= WATCH_MODEL=   # what the watchdog probes; default http://HOST:PORT and SERVED_NAME
# WATCH_PROBE=1 WATCH_PROBE_EVERY=180 WATCH_PROBE_TIMEOUT=30 WATCH_PROBE_FAILS=3   # the idle-only one-token probe
